From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] authz: a client context needs a resource manager (5909)

AuthzInitializeContextFromToken and AuthzInitializeContextFromSid (fast-b
3711) accepted a NULL resource manager. The documentation describes
hAuthzResourceManager as the manager creating the client context, and drafter
7's 5513 (dropped for 3711 by RECONCILE-CLOUD, which suggested considering
this) refused it with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER; its gate (test/authz-gate.sh,
check ctx-null-rm) is kept and now passes. Ported so that no behaviour of a
dropped implementation is lost (coordinator rule for duplicates).

Integration patch (integ-2026-10). Gates: authz (drafter 7), fastb-authz
(3711). Mutant SG_MUTANT_AUTHZ_NULL_RM.
---
diff --git a/dlls/authz/authz.c b/dlls/authz/authz.c
--- a/dlls/authz/authz.c
+++ b/dlls/authz/authz.c
@@ -498,7 +498,13 @@ BOOL WINAPI AuthzInitializeContextFromToken(DWORD flags, HANDLE token_handle,
         SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
         return FALSE;
     }
+    /* the client context belongs to the resource manager that creates it (docs: hAuthzResourceManager
+     * is the manager "creating this client context"); drafter 7's 5513 refused NULL, ported in 5909 */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_AUTHZ_NULL_RM
+    if (!rm || !valid_object( rm, MAGIC_RM ))
+#else
     if (rm && !valid_object( rm, MAGIC_RM ))
+#endif
     {
         SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
         return FALSE;
@@ -627,7 +633,13 @@ BOOL WINAPI AuthzInitializeContextFromSid(DWORD flags, PSID sid,
         SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_SID );
         return FALSE;
     }
+    /* the client context belongs to the resource manager that creates it (docs: hAuthzResourceManager
+     * is the manager "creating this client context"); drafter 7's 5513 refused NULL, ported in 5909 */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_AUTHZ_NULL_RM
+    if (!rm || !valid_object( rm, MAGIC_RM ))
+#else
     if (rm && !valid_object( rm, MAGIC_RM ))
+#endif
     {
         SetLastError( ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER );
         return FALSE;
